// requires. There is no *independent* machine referee: wikipron awa (0 lines) and kaikki Awadhi do not exist, and
// epitran ships no Awadhi (a clone would give the HINDI values anyway, so it would be circular). So `referees` is
// empty here — the 🔷 anchor lives in the hand-adjudicated gold (test/awadhi.test.ts): the sibilant merger
// श/ष→[s], the intervocalic flap ड→ɽ, व→[w], ऐ/औ→[ʌi]/[ʌu] — all from Saksena. NOT ⛔: Saksena is a real
// Awadhi-specific source, not a Hindi clone, so the anchor measures something. (A fuller Saksena-mined referee —
// the bho pattern — is a documented follow-up; the OCR IPA is corrupt so it needs visual reading.)
